Swap sort elements with memcpy in the bundled harfbuzz

hb_qsort's sort_r_swap exchanged elements one byte at a time. Under Fil-C,
a pointer keeps its capability only when copied as a whole word or by
memcpy; bytewise swaps leave each moved address paired with the other
element's capability. The face builder sorts (tag, {hb_blob_t *, order})
pairs this way, so hb.subset() / Face.blob trapped in compare_entries
("cannot read pointer with ptr < lower") in uharfbuzz's test_subset.

--- a/harfbuzz/src/hb-algs.hh
+++ b/harfbuzz/src/hb-algs.hh
@@ -1308,8 +1308,19 @@
 static inline void sort_r_swap(char *__restrict a, char *__restrict b,
                                size_t w)
 {
-  char tmp, *end = a+w;
-  for(; a < end; a++, b++) { SORT_R_SWAP(*a, *b, tmp); }
+  /* Swap through memcpy rather than byte by byte: under Fil-C, pointers
+     in the elements keep their capabilities only through word or memcpy
+     copies, and a bytewise swap leaves each address with the other
+     element's capability. */
+  alignas (16) char tmp[64];
+  while (w)
+  {
+    size_t n = w < sizeof (tmp) ? w : sizeof (tmp);
+    memcpy (tmp, a, n);
+    memcpy (a, b, n);
+    memcpy (b, tmp, n);
+    a += n; b += n; w -= n;
+  }
 }
 
 /* swap a, b iff a>b */
